# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repository, check out the native
# form on each platform.
#
# Added 2026-09-26, after a merge conflict where both sides of bmi.py were
# textually identical -- the local commit held LF (277 bytes, git had converted
# it via core.autocrlf=true) while the file uploaded through GitHub's web UI
# held CRLF (296 bytes, the raw bytes the browser sent). Git saw two different
# blobs and refused to merge them.
#
# With this file present, git normalises on the way in, so that class of
# conflict cannot happen again.
* text=auto
